#====================================================================
# Draft: License-restricted second source injected at build time -
#        wrapper tarball + vendor archive both in conandata sources,
#        Makefile unpacks/patches vendor code (FreeBSD-port style,
#        libamrnb 11.0.0.0 26104-b00.zip)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-13502-LIBAMRNB-DUAL-SOURCE-RESTRICTED-ARCHIVE
trigger_tool:           configure|make|autotools
phase:                  configuration
error_signature:        You need unzip utility to prepare sources|You need patch utility to prepare sources|26104-b00_ANSI_C_source_code\.zip|prepare_sources\.sh

severity:               1
category:               build-system, autotools, portability, sources, ohos
match_keywords:         dual source, restricted license, 3GPP, prepare_sources.sh, DIST_SUBDIR, FreeBSD port, wrapper tarball, build-time unpack, unzip, AC_PATH_PROG, conandata sources list, download(), strip_root, in-tree build, top_srcdir

title:                  Recipes for wrapper-plus-restricted-vendor-code projects (amrnb/amrwb style) declare BOTH archives in conandata sources, keep the vendor zip packed in source() and copy the whole tree to build_folder for an in-tree build so the Makefile's own prepare step (unzip+patch+sed) regenerates vendor sources into a disposable copy

root_cause:             Some codec wrappers (penguin.cz amrnb/amrwb for 3GPP TS 26.104/26.204) ship only the autotools skeleton; the actual vendor code arrives as a separate license-restricted archive (3GPP zips are not mirrored by any distro) that must sit next to configure before make. configure hard-probes host tools unzip and patch (AC_PATH_PROG + AC_MSG_ERROR when absent and sources not yet prepared), and the Makefile regenerates the vendor .c/.h into $(top_srcdir), mutating the source tree.

affected_scope:         autotools packages whose real sources are injected at build time from a second archive. Verified: libamrnb 11.0.0.0 (26104-b00.zip, 9 CLI tools + libamrnb). Expected same for libamrwb 11.0.0.0 (26204-b00.zip) and any FreeBSD-style DIST_SUBDIR port with restricted sources.

verification_cmd:       conan create archives/l/libamrnb/11.0.0.0 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           dual-conandata-entry-plus-intree-build-copy
rec_description:        (1) conandata.yml lists TWO source entries (wrapper tarball, vendor zip) each with url list + sha256; source() does get(entry0, strip_root=True) then download(entry1.url, "<vendor>.zip", sha256=...) so the zip stays packed in the source folder. (2) build() copies the pristine source tree (wrapper + zip) into self.build_folder and builds in-tree - the Makefile's prepare rule then unpacks/applies patches inside the disposable copy, keeping the conan source cache clean. (3) build() asserts the zip landed with its exact expected size (427897 for 26104-b00.zip) to catch WAF-page poisoning at a readable point. (4) make -j1: the prepare chain is upstream's own serialization point. (5) Host tool deps (bash/unzip/patch/sed/tr) must be probed on the build host before CI (configure errors out otherwise); OHOS real devices: unzip was missing on one lab machine - check command -v unzip patch first.
rec_command:            grep -n "download(self" archives/l/libamrnb/11.0.0.0/conanfile.py && grep -n "copy(self" archives/l/libamrnb/11.0.0.0/conanfile.py
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               archives/l/libamrnb/11.0.0.0/conanfile.py (source/build methods) + conandata.yml dual entries

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      preprepared-vendor-tree-in-exports_sources
fallback_description:   Pre-running prepare and shipping the generated vendor .c/.h via exports_sources avoids host unzip/patch deps but redistributes license-restricted vendor code inside the recipe repo - rejected for 3GPP material (this is exactly why distros refuse to mirror it). Only acceptable for freely licensed vendors.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       commit vendor restricted sources into the repo|repack vendor zip into recipe
forbid_1_reason:        3GPP reference code carries a restrictive license (FreeBSD marks such ports RESTRICTED; no distro mirrors the archives). PF2 also blocks archives in the repo.
forbid_1_consequence:   License violation in the public recipe repo; JC3/PF2 gate rejection.

principles:             minimal-patch, keep-source-cache-clean, declared-dependency-metadata, real-evidence-over-assumption
